15509 0 obj
  << /ActualText (AI agents\054 APIs\054 and applications to exchange value as freely as they exchange data\056 Early participants and supporters include Amazon Web Services\054 Microsoft\054 Google\054 Cloudflare\054 KakaoPay\054 Mastercard\054 Visa\054 Stripe\054 Circle\054 the Solana Foundation\054 and Shopify \024 spanning cloud infrastructure\054 payments\054 blockchain\054 and commerce\056\n\nBefore that announcement\054 in February 2026\054 Bitcoin\047s Lightning Labs released an open\055source toolkit for AI agents and put forward L402 as a competing payment layer\0568\056 Google\047s Agent Payments Protocol \050AP2\0519\056 and the Machine Payments Protocol \050MPP\051 from Stripe and Tempo10\056 have since joined the field\054 making the contest over payment standards for the machine economy a full\055blown race\056\n\nThis report begins by mapping that race\054 but its deeper aim is to surface the larger transformation unfolding beneath it\056 What is happening now is not simply a technical competition between payment protocols\056 The core shift is that the entire infrastructure of the internet economy is being redesigned \024 from one built on human identity to one built on cryptographic keys\056 The rules of payment are being rewritten from the ground up\056\n\nThe report proceeds in order\072 from the awakening of HTTP 402 \024 a status code reserved but unused for thirty years \024 through the long failure of micropayments\054 the migration of payment eligibility from identity to key\054 the competition between x402 and L402\054 the reserve currency problem of the machine economy\054 and finally the challenges facing Korea\047s payment industry in the middle of this transition\056 The starting point is a small blank space\054 reserved thirty years ago in the internet\047s original blueprint\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 15510 0 R
     /Pg 1770 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

