15553 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The significance of that gap becomes clearer when you trace the web\047s history\056 In many ways\054 the story of the web is the story of users gradually winning back capabilities that were never theirs to begin with\056 The web of the 1990s was a reading medium\0562\051 Users were essentially readers of pages others had built\073 the internet functioned like an enormous library\056 When Web 2\0560 took hold in the mid\0552000s\054 users gained the ability to write\056 Blogging\054 uploading to YouTube\054 sharing on Instagram became everyday activities\056 But this writing revolution left two problems unsolved\056 The first was ownership\072 the content and data that users created on platforms never truly came back to them\056 The second was payment\072 users could create content\054 but the ability to price that content and collect payment per request never became a native feature of the web itself\056\n\nThe first problem \024 ownership \024 was the central agenda of Web3\054 the vision of the web built on blockchain and smart contracts\056 Vitalik Buterin\047s oft\055cited World of Warcraft anecdote captures this well\056 When a skill belonging to a character he loved was suddenly nerfed\054 he recalled realizing \042how horrific centralized services could be\056\04214\056 Blockchain and smart contracts drew their      \176)
     /K [ 8 ]
     /P 15554 0 R
     /Pg 2536 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

