15574 0 obj
  << /ActualText (energy from a technological imagination aimed at breaking up that unilateral power\056 From the mid\0552010s onward\054 Ethereum became a testing ground for NFTs asserting the uniqueness of digital content\054 ERC\05520 tokens defining a standard for fungible assets\054 and DAOs experimenting with collective ownership and governance\056 The promise that what users created could belong to users began to take concrete technical form\056\n\nYet even as Ethereum\047s NFTs and tokens addressed the ownership gap\054 the payment gap remained unfilled\056 Assets could be placed on a blockchain\054 but that didn\047t create a natural flow of commerce at the level of individual web requests\056 We gained the ability to create content and to own it \024 but pricing a webpage visit or an API call\054 and collecting payment for each one\054 still required a separate checkout page\054 a login\054 and a card transaction\056 Ownership is a state that persists between acquisition and disposal\073 payment is a procedure that demands a fresh cycle of authorization\054 transfer\054 and settlement with every single request\056 Changing how ownership worked did not automatically change how payment worked\056 Web3 made real progress on the question of who owns what \024 but the question of how value flows in real time\054 request by request\054 remained open\056)
     /K [ 8 ]
     /P 15575 0 R
