15583 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Circle\054 USDT issued by Tether \024 built up a market footprint through the first half of the 2020s substantial enough to earn the name \042digital dollars\056\042 The significance of this goes beyond the fact that dollar\055denominated assets can now move across blockchains and across borders\056 Dollar stablecoins have transformed dollar\055denominated value into a digital token that programs can recognize\054 divide\054 and automatically settle\056 USDC\054 in particular\054 supports precision to six decimal places \024 meaning a program can work directly with units as small as \0440\056000001\056 Given that card payment systems have in practice been unable to process transactions meaningfully below a few tens of cents\054 stablecoins represent a structurally different kind of payment instrument\072 dollar\055stable in denomination\054 yet programmable at a granularity that cards cannot approach\056\n\nRemove any one of these three forces and the payment gap could not be filled\056 Without blockchain and smart contracts\054 the idea of executing payments and settlements programmatically on an open network would have remained abstract\056 Without AI\054 there would be no non\055human actor capable of generating requests\054 evaluating costs\054 and executing payments automatically at a speed and frequency beyond human reach\056 And without stablecoins\054 that actor would have no stable currency to work with\056 The actor to execute payment\054 the currency for that actor to use\054 and the rails for that currency to flow \024 all three came together in the mid\0552020s\056 Coinbase\047s publication of the x402 specification in May 2025\054 and the Linux Foundation\047s launch of the x402 Foundation in April 2026\054 are the visible events marking the point where these three forces converged\056 HTTP 402 \024 reserved and dormant for so long \024 awoke precisely at that confluence\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 15584 0 R
     /Pg 3270 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
