15647 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Every moment in the modern payment system \024 built on credit and accounts \024 has always run alongside a procedure for confirming who is paying\056 The merchant\047s signature on a bill of exchange\054 the handwriting on a check\054 the ID presented at a bank counter\054 the PIN entered at an ATM\054 the CVV typed into an online checkout form\054 the biometric scan on a mobile app \024 this long list has always carried the same demand\072 prove that you are a real\054 existing human being who can be held responsible for this transaction\056 The Bank Secrecy Act of 1970 and the Know Your Customer frameworks that followed institutionalized this demand in law\0567\051 After the September 11 attacks\054 international anti\055money laundering regimes tightened further\054 binding bank account access and financial services to ever more rigorous identity verification\056 In the language of finance\072 the modern payment system is\054 at its core\054 a system for confirming the existence of a responsible human actor\056\n\nThe credit card is the most compressed expression of this verification framework\056 A single card carries the result of the issuer\047s identity and creditworthiness check on the cardholder\054 and the card number and CVV re\055invoke that result at every transaction\056 The account registration\054 email verification\054 phone verification\054 and one\055time passwords required every time you sign up for a new service repeat and reinforce the same proof\056 In the world of B2B APIs\054 this proof takes the abstracted form of an API key23\056 \024 essentially a declaration that \042the caller presenting this key is an authorized caller connected to a pre\055registered account or organization\056\042 The service provider receives that declaration and permits or rejects the call accordingly\056 If a key is lost\054 calls through that key become impossible\073 if it is exposed and revoked\054 the access rights tied to it are cut off along with it\056 Identity\054 account\054 and permission are all bound together within a single management system\056\n\nThis lengthy chain of verification produced a payment experience that is deeply human\055centric\056 A person visits a webpage\054 enters card details\054 clicks confirm\054 receives an OTP\054 enters the code\054 and sees a success message\056 Every step assumes the physical presence and cognitive engagement of a human user \024 mouse clicks\054 screen taps\054 passwords\054 biometric scans\056 And for decades\054 this human\055centric payment experience worked efficiently\056 But that efficiency held only under one condition\072 that the party making the payment was a person\056 The moment the actor sending a payment request is a software agent rather than a human\054 a UX designed to call on human hands and eyes stops being a bridge to payment and becomes a wall in front of it\056)
     /K [ 5 ]
     /P 15648 0 R
     /Pg 4460 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

