15703 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Looking at the competition to build the machine economy\047s payment layer\054 two distinct design philosophies emerge \024 both built around the same status code 402\054 but centering on different payment assets\056 x402 takes stablecoins like USDC as its primary payment asset\054 aiming to standardize payment at the level of individual HTTP requests\056 L402 takes the Bitcoin Lightning Network as its backbone\054 combining payment with access authorization\056 The two designs offer different answers to the question of how machine economy payments should work\054 but share the same core principle\072 payment should be part of the request itself\054 not a separate page\054 and access to paid resources should require nothing more than a wallet and a signature \024 no account\054 no card registration\056\n\nThe x402 flow works as follows\056 A client \024 human or agent \024 sends an HTTP request to a paid API or digital resource\05625\056 Under normal circumstances the server would respond with 200 OK\054 but if the endpoint is paywalled it returns 402 Payment Required instead\056 This 402 response carries the information needed to complete payment\072 the amount required\054 the wallet address to pay\054 the accepted payment methods\054 and the mechanism for proving payment\056 The client uses this information to generate a stablecoin payment payload8\051 and sends it in the header of a second request\056 The server can verify and settle the payment directly\054 or delegate that process to a facilitator\0569\051 Once the payment conditions are met and settlement is confirmed\054 the server returns 200 OK along with the requested resource\056 Using a fast network and a facilitator\054 this entire process can complete in anywhere from a few hundred milliseconds to a few seconds\056 No login\054 no registration\054 no card number\056 The request itself is the unit of payment\054 and proof of payment is the access credential\056 If x402\047s philosophy could be compressed into a single formula\054 it would be\072 Payment \075 Access\056\n)
     /K [ 7 ]
     /P 15704 0 R
     /Pg 5388 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

