15727 0 obj
  << /ActualText (actual usage \024 suited to services where costs vary per request\054 such as LLM token counts\054 compute time\054 or bytes transferred\05627\056 For high\055frequency small payments\054 a separate batch\055settlement scheme is also proposed\05628\056 Rather than committing every request to the blockchain immediately\054 this approach uses escrow and off\055chain vouchers to bundle multiple payments for settlement together\056 The buyer deposits funds into escrow upfront\054 then signs a voucher recording cumulative usage with each request\056 The seller verifies the voucher and provides the service\054 later submitting multiple vouchers together for on\055chain settlement\056 This is well suited to scenarios like repeated paid API calls or usage\055based endpoints where settling each small payment individually would be too costly or too slow\056\n\nWorth noting in x402\047s economic model is the role of the facilitator\056 The facilitator is an intermediary that shields the server from the complexity of blockchain operations\056 As mentioned\054 the server can call the blockchain and verify signatures directly\054 or delegate that work to a facilitator \024 meaning sellers can accept x402 payments without building their own blockchain integration\054 verification logic\054 or settlement infrastructure\056 This is one of the key conditions enabling x402 to spread\056 If every API provider or content business had to build its own wallet infrastructure\054 on\055chain settlement\054 and payment verification logic\054 the barrier to adopting x402 would rise sharply\056 The facilitator is the layer that lowers that barrier\056\n\nAs of April 2026\054 the most prominently referenced facilitator in the x402 ecosystem is Coinbase\047s CDP \050Coinbase Developer Platform\051 facilitator\056 According to CDP documentation\054 the facilitator is free for up to 1\054000 transactions per month\054 with a fee of \0440\056001 per transaction thereafter\05629\056 Network gas fees are paid separately on\055chain\056 x402 is not\054 therefore\054 a free payment network in any absolute sense \024 it is more accurately described as a usage\055based payment infrastructure that structures costs differently from traditional card payment\056 That said\054 with card payment\047s flat fee running at around \0440\05630 per transaction\054 the CDP facilitator\047s \0440\056001 per transaction fee is three hundred times smaller\056 The cost doesn\047t disappear\054 but the room to operate at far smaller payment units becomes substantial\056\n\nx402\047s rate of adoption has been unusual by the standards of payment protocol history\056 From its launch in May 2025 through the end of that year\054 the protocol processed over 14 million cumulative transactions with a cumulative value exceeding \04410 million\05630\056 But more significant than those numbers is the institutional move\072 x402\047s transfer to the Linux Foundation as an open\055source project under neutral governance signals that it is no longer just a Coinbase experiment but a protocol seeking to become an industry standard\056 This does not mean\054 however\054 that the revival of 402 spells a stablecoin monopoly\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 15728 0 R
     /Pg 5980 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
