15782 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The agent payment ecosystem is indeed developing toward coexistence of multiple frameworks and payment methods rather than rapid convergence on a single protocol or rail\056 That said\054 as of May 2026\054 the early institutional and developer momentum is forming around x402 and dollar stablecoin\055based payment\056 Large infrastructure players \024 Coinbase\054 Cloudflare\054 AWS\054 Microsoft \024 are actively participating in the emerging standard competition for agent and machine\055to\055machine payments\054 and dollar stablecoins like USDC sit at the center of that movement\056 Even as multiple protocols and frameworks coexist\054 stablecoin\055based payment is gaining the earliest traction in the market\056\n\nx402\047s strength lies in the simplicity of payment execution\056 By directly binding HTTP requests to payment\054 it folds the procedure for accessing a paid resource and the procedure for paying for it into a single flow\056 The availability of facilitators \024 allowing sellers to handle payment verification and settlement without running their own blockchain infrastructure \024 also works in its favor for early adoption\056 In short\054 x402 makes it relatively straightforward for developers to handle per\055request payment within the familiar conventions of the web\056\n\nBut this momentum cannot be explained by technical convenience alone\056 Stablecoins are fast\054 programmable\054 and easy to connect to existing financial institutions\056 More importantly\054 the world\047s financial system still runs on the dollar\056 Dollar stablecoins move on blockchains\054 but their unit of account remains the dollar \024 a powerful advantage in a machine economy where agents and services must transact across borders\056 A stablecoin is not just a fast digital token\073 it is a programmable dollar\054 and that is precisely why it is well positioned to become the early payment medium of the machine economy\056\n\nThis doesn\047t mean the ecosystem will fully converge on a single payment rail\056 Service providers can support multiple payment methods simultaneously\054 and clients can select the appropriate rail based on their wallet configuration and policies\056 The scene of a human user choosing between card\054 bank transfer\054 and mobile payment at checkout may be replicated inside an agent\047s wallet and policy engine\056 But the selection criteria will no longer be just user familiarity\056 Agents will choose payment rails by weighing cost\054 speed\054 stability\054 liquidity\054 regulatory risk\054 and the nature of the underlying collateral\056 Services that prioritize stability and broad ecosystem support will likely favor x402 and stablecoin payment\073 those that prioritize neutrality and the independence of Bitcoin\055based payment may choose L402\056\n\nThe machine economy\047s payment landscape is unlikely to be fully resolved by a single technical standard or a single payment rail\056 But the fact that today\047s           \176)
