15806 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The diagnosis that stablecoins are emerging as the machine economy\047s common payment medium is\054 as a factual observation\054 hard to dispute\056 In terms of speed\054 programmability\054 dollar\055denominated stability\054 and regulatory acceptance\054 today\047s stablecoins are more convenient than any other digital currency as a payment instrument\056 But convenience as a payment medium does not automatically confer suitability as a reserve currency for the machine economy\056 As of 2026\054 the global stablecoin market has exceeded \044300 billion\054 with two tokens \024 issued by Tether and Circle \024 accounting for over 90\045 of the total market\05636\056 This concentration illustrates stablecoins\047 strengths clearly\054 but it also reveals precisely where their limitations come from\056\n\nThe first limitation is the issuer\056 The 1\0721 dollar value of USDC and USDT is not maintained by pure market consensus \024 it is underpinned by the reserves the issuers hold and their promise to redeem\056 Those reserves must be composed of safe assets\054 redemption must be possible when needed\054 and that promise must command market trust\056 When Silicon Valley Bank failed in March 2023\054 USDC briefly broke its dollar peg amid concerns that \0443\0563 billion in reserves held at the bank could be frozen or impaired\05637\056 The peg recovered within days\054 but the episode exposed something important\072 the stability that the name \042stablecoin\042 promises ultimately rests on a piece of the traditional financial system\056 Issuer insolvency\054 reserve quality\054 and unexpected bank runs are structural risks that stablecoins can face at any time\056\n\nDollar stablecoins circulate on blockchains\054 but their issuance\054 custody\054 and redemption are difficult to insulate from specific financial regulatory regimes\056 USDC in particular\054 tightly connected to the US financial system\054 is directly exposed to decisions by US regulators\056 When the US Treasury\047s Office of Foreign Assets Control \050OFAC\051 sanctioned Tornado Cash\054 an Ethereum\055based mixer service\054 in August 2022\054 Circle froze USDC held at OFAC\055designated addresses\05638\056 It was an instance of a political decision in one jurisdiction limiting the transferability of on\055chain assets through an issuer\047s freeze authority\056 That capability is useful for preventing money laundering\054 but it also demonstrates that stablecoins are not fully neutral assets\056 Their usability can change depending on the regulatory environment and political decisions in the jurisdiction where the issuer operates\056 The deeper the machine economy\047s         \176)
     /K [ 5 ]
     /P 15807 0 R
     /Pg 7178 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

