15858 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Building the payment infrastructure for the machine economy does not bring the discussion to an end\056 The moment payment becomes possible\054 a new set of questions immediately follows\056 Who bears responsibility for the actions of the agent carrying out that payment\077 How should the data accessed by those agents be priced\077 And how will the payment industries of different countries adapt to this new structure\077\n\nTechnical protocols may solve the problem of payment execution\054 but for those systems to become embedded within society\054 legal accountability\054 data markets\054 and the restructuring of industrial infrastructure must all be addressed alongside them\056 Chapter 6 examines these three ramifications in turn\056)
