15871 0 obj
  << /ActualText (oversight are gradually being addressed\056 Yet these efforts remain largely focused on clarifying the responsibilities of the humans and corporations deploying AI systems\054 rather than moving toward granting independent legal status to the agents themselves\056\n\nOf course\054 the idea of extending legal personality to non\055human entities is not entirely unfamiliar\056 Modern capitalism has long granted economic and legal standing to non\055human entities through the institution of the corporation\056 But corporations are built on the assumption that they ultimately operate through the intentions and organizational structures of natural persons\056 Agents challenge that assumption\056\n\nAn agent may still have a natural person or corporation behind it\054 but that party does not directly instruct or verify every action the agent takes in real time\056 Today\047s agents generally operate within predefined permissions and control frameworks\054 but as the number of agents increases \024 and as the frequency and complexity of their transactions continue to grow \024 supervising every action in real time and clearly assigning responsibility afterward will become progressively more difficult\056 It is precisely this widening gap between controllability and accountability that demands a new institutional framework\056\nRealistically\054 the first mechanism likely to emerge will be some form of institutionalized agent ID\072 assigning every agent a unique cryptographic identifier and enabling the long\055term verification of the transaction history tied to the wallet associated with that identifier\056 This would not make agents citizens\056 Rather\054 it would function as an institutional mechanism for efficiently determining responsibility for the transactions agents generate\056\n\nIf systems evolve in this direction\054 the economic activity of agents will belong not to the realm of anonymous freedom\054 but to a regime of traceable autonomy\056 In the end\054 the central challenge facing the next chapter of digital citizenship is how to design autonomy and traceability together\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 15872 0 R
     /Pg 8550 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
