15879 0 obj
  << /ActualText (One of the most immediate consequences enabled by x402 and L402 is the pricing structure of public web data\056 Ever since search engines and web crawlers began collecting public pages across the internet\054 the large\055scale free use of public web data has functioned as an implicit assumption of the internet economy\056 But AI training is changing the nature of that assumption\056\n\nWhen data collected for free is used to train AI models\054 and those models are then sold as paid services\054 data producers increasingly see the arrangement as a clear transfer of value\056 Since 2023\054 copyright lawsuits brought by The New York Times against OpenAI and Microsoft\05442\056 along with moves by publishers and media organizations to block AI crawlers from accessing their content\054 have made this structural tension increasingly visible\05643\056\n\nCloudflare\047s pay\055per\055crawl experiment\054 introduced in mid\0552025\054 represents an attempt to resolve this tension in a new way\05644\056 The service allows website operators to decide for themselves whether to permit crawler access and at what price\056 When a crawler attempts access\054 the site returns an HTTP 402 response\054 and the crawler must either accept the price and pay or abandon access altogether\056 This is one of the most intuitive examples of how x402           \176)
     /K [ 4 ]
     /P 15880 0 R
     /Pg 8550 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

