15900 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The fact that KakaoPay appeared among the companies expressing early support and participation in the launch announcement of the x402 Foundation should not be dismissed lightly\05614\051 KakaoPay\047s participation can be read as an attempt by Korea\047s payment industry to engage early in the international discussion surrounding the transition toward machine\055payment infrastructure\056 But early participation alone does not secure leadership\056 The domestic challenges that follow participation remain substantial\056\n\nThe first challenge is the regulatory environment\056 Korea\047s Virtual Asset User Protection Act\054 which took effect in 2024\054 established the basic framework for virtual\055asset transactions within Korea\05615\051 Yet detailed rules governing the issuance of stablecoins and their use as payment instruments remain incomplete\056 During this transitional period\054 Korean companies are likely either to rely on stablecoins issued abroad or to design hybrid structures that do not fully depart from traditional payment rails for domestic transactions\056 How this awkward interim period is managed will shape the early form of Korea\047s machine economy\056\n\nThe second challenge is wallet user experience\056 The philosophy of x402 is \042access through wallets without accounts\054\042 but the reality in 2026 is that             \176)
     /K [ 8 ]
     /P 15901 0 R
