15905 0 obj
  << /ActualText (wallets have not yet become universal for ordinary users\056 In particular\054 the user experience of non\055custodial wallets in the consumer market remains significantly less convenient than conventional card payments or simplified mobile payment services\056\n\nKakaoPay\047s greatest asset is its massive user base and the payment experience those users are already familiar with\056 The next phase of competition in Korea\047s payment market will depend on how effectively stablecoin payments and x402\055based payments can be integrated into that existing user experience with minimal friction\056 Supporting the protocol itself will not be enough\056 The experience must become so seamless that users may not even realize they are making payments through x402\056\n\nThe third challenge is refunds and accounting\056 Under the x402 structure\054 traditional card\055style chargebacks are not inherently supported\056 Once payment is finalized on a blockchain\054 it becomes difficult to apply the post\055transaction reversals and chargeback mechanisms used by card networks\056 Situations requiring refunds would instead need separate transfers or escrow\055based smart contract logic layered on top\056\n\nFrom a consumer\055protection perspective\054 this is an inconvenient structure\056 From an accounting perspective\054 companies processing hundreds of thousands of small monthly transactions would also require systems fundamentally different from those used in traditional payment networks when aggregating payments and recognizing revenue\056\n\nFor this reason\054 x402 is unlikely to succeed by replacing all payments outright\056 Consumer\055facing commerce involving shopping\055cart payments\054 subscriptions\054 and complex refund scenarios will likely continue to rely on simplified payment platforms such as KakaoPay\054 Apple Pay\054 and Google Pay\056 x402\054 by contrast\054 is more likely to spread throughout backend domains such as machine\055to\055machine API calls\054 data access\054 and intellectual\055property licensing\056\n\nIn other words\054 a division of labor may emerge in which simplified payment services handle the front end while x402 operates primarily in backend infrastructure\056 The challenge facing Korea\047s payment industry is to design the underlying infrastructure capable of handling refunds\054 accounting\054 and user experience at the intersection of these two systems\056\nIf Korean companies solve this challenge effectively\054 they may be able to lead the East Asian market during the expansion of this new payment rail\056 If not\054 they risk once again remaining followers rather than leaders\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 15906 0 R
     /Pg 9152 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

